WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.303
This is the technical deep
dive for Book 05 of the

2
00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:07.125
Federal Modernization Workbook,
Devices and Endpoints.

3
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:10.901
It's for the architects and
engineers who move a domain-joined

4
00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.862
fleet onto Intune, and its
servers onto Azure Arc.

5
00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:16.936
It comes in two parts of about
twenty-five minutes each,

6
00:00:16.936 --> 00:00:19.326
and four modules you can watch separately.

7
00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:21.037
Part 1 is the endpoints.

8
00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:24.869
First, how a new device is governed
from the moment it powers on,

9
00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:29.075
and the three paths an existing estate
can take to the same end state.

10
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:34.330
Then the Group Policy sunset: how
every GPO is inventoried, classified,

11
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.950
replaced and retired, and the
policy library that replaces it.

12
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.102
Part 2 is servers and the run state:

13
00:00:41.102 --> 00:00:44.715
bringing servers under Azure
Arc with a day-one baseline,

14
00:00:44.715 --> 00:00:49.788
and then operating and evidencing the
whole fleet once Intune is the authority.

15
00:00:49.788 --> 00:00:53.538
The slides show tables,
flows and decision matrices.

16
00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:57.390
The scripts and policy payloads live
in the chapters and in Appendix A;

17
00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.774
they're marked there as illustrative and
untested against a production tenant,

18
00:01:01.774 --> 00:01:04.820
and I'll point you to them
rather than put them on screen.
